  "question": "What anonymous first-party public service controls does the current NLC Wenjin detail page expose for the 2004 《文汇报》 1938-1999 / 13-DVD item, and do any of them provide a direct public page-level route without account action?",
  "answer": "The anonymous detail page visibly exposes online-reading, document-delivery and holdings controls, but no direct page-level newspaper object is recovered. The document-delivery control is a POST form to the NLC document-delivery gateway and is not submitted. The page source emits an SSO-wrapped OPAC item link whose inner catalog locator is NLC01 / 002860236; because the page deliberately wraps it in SSO, the inner OPAC URL is recorded as a catalog cross-anchor but not bypassed or executed. The source-emitted rdDetails.js client logic is login-state dependent: online-reading resolution uses uri/directLink/VPN variables only after login-state handling, and the anonymous page displays the login-required marker. No login, VPN, SSO, POST, document-delivery submission or online-reading action is executed.",
